## Grooming looks exactly like stagnation

A bulk move into the queued column stamps a fresh entry date on every issue it
touches, so "stuck" counts include freshly groomed work unless you cut it off.
Set the cutoff too early and you hide real stagnation instead.

Before reporting a stuck count, group the parked issues by (entry date, author).
One date plus one author across many issues is a grooming batch, not a queue that
has stopped moving.

